<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.AFRICAN AUG PRODUCER PRICE INDEX UP 7.4 PCT Y/Y.</title>
<headline>S.AFRICAN AUG PRODUCER PRICE INDEX UP 7.4 PCT Y/Y.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's all-commodities producer price index rose 1.0 percent in August from July after rising 0.8 percent in July, Central Statistical Service figures show.</p>
<p>The year-on-year rise in August was 7.4 percent after July's 6.6 percent rise.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economists forecast PPI would rise 0.9 percent month-on-month and 7.2 percent year-on-year.  </p>
<p>    Pct changes:	     Year/year		    month/month</p>
<p>			 Aug '96   Jul '96   Aug '95  - latest   prev</p>
<p>All commodities    7.4	 6.6	 7.8	  1.0	0.8</p>
<p>Locally produced   8.5	 7.3	 8.1	  1.4	1.1</p>
<p>Imported	     4.5	 4.9	 5.8	  0.1	0.0</p>
<p>Index (base 1995=100):</p>
<p>			 Aug '96   Jul '96   Aug '95</p>
<p>All commodities    108.0     106.9     100.6</p>
<p>Locally produced   109.2     107.7     100.6</p>
<p>Imported	     104.8     104.7     100.3</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
